    "K_t": "Evidence:\n[1] The film, also known as \"Enemy Agent\", was released in the United States in January 1940.\n[2] George Michael Cohan (July 3, 1878November 5, 1942), known professionally as George M. Cohan, was an American entertainer, playwright, composer, lyricist, actor, singer, dancer and producer.\n[3] Boris Karloff played Jonathan Brewster, who \"looks like Karloff,\" on the Broadway stage, but he was unable to do the movie as well because he was still appearing in the play during filming, and Raymond Massey took his place.\n[4] It was directed by Terry O. Morse and stars Boris Karloff and Margaret Lindsay."
